[Music]  nfts even if you don't know what  non-fungible tokens are and i will get  to that you've probably seen talk of  them floating around the internet and  now  nfts are coming for cars  tonale is the first car ever equipped a  blockchain not fungible token yep the  new alfa romeo tanale suv will come with  its own nft but we're not talking about  some kind of collectible digital artwork  of the car so how could the auto  industry use blockchain technology and  are car nfts a passing fad or here to  stay let's find out  [Music]  okay first what is an nft the super  simplified version is that a  non-fungible token is basically a unique  one-of-a-kind certificate that can store  information the important part is that  token can be authenticated using the  blockchain a decentralized network of  computers that no one person owns but  anyone can access that can verify or  disprove that a token is what it claims  to be  famously nfts have been used as proof of  ownership of the original of an easily  replicated digital collectible take this  board api club site that sells images of  yep board apes for literally hundreds of  thousands of dollars now while there is  absolutely nothing stopping me from  downloading this image i'd just be  downloading a copy the nft is used to  say who has the original like a  certificate that comes with a piece of  art but alfa romeo is focusing less on  the art side and more on that  certification side come with me i'll  explain  [Music]  so this is the service book for my car  and it's basically a paper history of  the life of the vehicle every time i  take my car to the garage they stamp  this book with the work that was carried  out and how many miles were on the clock  and they do that so that when i come to  sell the vehicle there is an authentic  record that i can show a prospective  buyer  even if i didn't have that paper record  there are companies that collect data  from the dmv law enforcement agencies  and insurers to generate a car's history  which prospective buyers can look up  online but what alfa romeo is proposing  is that some of that information could  go directly from the car and onto an nft  each nft is associated to one specific  vehicle and only one the car gators  information directly from the car's  electronic system and recovers all data  on the blockchain the idea is that if  the driver chooses to data like service  history and mileage could be uploaded to  an nft which the driver could then show  a prospective buyer to have the  certainty that you have a data stored  elsewhere non-corruptible not manageable  by the dealer by the fleet by the oem  even that certifies the fact that you  have a certain mileage and nobody can  change that it's something that first  reassures who's buying and of course on  the other side also who's who's selling  now when i spoke to alfa romeo they  couldn't really tell me how much it  would cost to update that nft or what  platform the nft would be hosted on  sorry crypto nerds but while they're not  revealing pricing for now they said  they're working with their blockchain  provider to limit costs and that the nft  might be available at no extra fee for  the customer so could car nfts work well  at the heart of it nfts were designed as  a secure way to store and verify data as  cars are becoming smarter they're  becoming more able to generate and  capture that data for things like  whether the airbags have gone off or  whether there's been sharp braking or  how many times the batteries have been  recharged technically all of that data  could in theory be stored on an nft if  you chose to but what's not clear is  whether this will catch on stalantis who  own alfa romeo told me that nfts would  be rolled out to other cars in the alfa  romeo range and the other brands under  the stellantis flag may follow but in  order for nfts to become widespread  across the auto industry it's likely  that drivers mechanics dealerships and  other automakers are going to have to  learn how to read write store and  transfer those nfts and be willing to  pay for the process and we haven't even  begun to talk about some of the  environmental impact of these nfts so  even if your next set of wheels comes  with its own minted nft i'd hang onto  those paper documents for now  so would you like your next card to come  with an nft let me know in the comments  below and as always if you're interested  in the future of how we might be getting  from a to b then don't forget to  subscribe see you soon

